    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d609">

                <pb facs="0740" n="628" xml:id="pg628"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.515/801</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum by the Under Secretary of State</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Phillips</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1935-10-29">October 29, 1935</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>The Chinese Ambassador told me that he had called last evening upon Secretary
                    Morgenthau to inform him confidentially that the Chinese Government desired to
                    sell 100,000,000 ounces of silver in two 50,000,000 lots. Mr. Morgenthau replied
                    that he would give the matter consideration, would speak to the President, and
                    would give him an answer later.</p>
                <p>The Ambassador was particularly anxious that the State Department should know of
                    the step which he had taken in the conference with Mr. Morgenthau.</p>
                <p>Mr. Morgenthau has asked the Ambassador to secure for him information with regard
                    to China’s financial program.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">William Phillips</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
